\begin{abstract}
We compute the intrinsic class-two section obstruction for the Fermat cubic with its nine coordinate cusps removed, including its integral residue complex, path origins, restricted convergence, and lifting fibers. We construct an actual obstruction invisible locally and at every finite coefficient level; refute the two proposed class-two inertia restrictions; and prove the pro-three cyclotomic centralizer criterion. Finite arithmetic field and cocycle constructions give the exact full, metabelian and marked-depth images and all their fibers, with compatibility for arbitrary ramification support. An explicit section at seventeen has the literal local cusp restriction and a global class-three lift, but no class-four lift. We identify the inherited quotient maps and every marked coefficient layer integrally. Over every number field we give the complete arithmetic obstruction test, restriction and descent maps, and the class-two germ classification, including finite algebraic formulas for every point's central coordinates. The three requested full local profinite fixed groups are computed through an explicit valuation and stabilizer comparison. Parts A, B, C, D and F are complete. Every multiplier-one pronilpotent peripheral automorphism lifts to the full profinite source with all prescribed conjugators. The actual special image has dimension three in weight five, and the actual gentle invariant image has dimension two in weight nine, for every prime $\ell\ge5$. We construct a full gentle pair in the extra weight-nine direction and prove that it fails the pentagon. The relative lifting theorem constructs an actual full gentle pair in the extra complex-multiplication coset, with the exact positive CM bits $(1,0)$ and every prescribed finite conjugator retained. Task E.2 is complete. The full pentagon question E.3 remains under investigation. We compute the elementary abelian peripheral lifting obstruction, its exact covering restriction, and coupled finite central counterexamples. Every finite $A_5$ chief extension has a positive generating-lift count preserved under the specified peripheral base maps. A split $A_6$ chief extension has an ordinary generating-lift obstruction, with every centralizer choice retained; explicit outer-image conditions give complementary lifting theorems. The joint binary and ternary degree-six braid refinement retains all twenty-four CM candidates and $864$ finite points, all of which pass the full-target periodic-braid conjugacy tests. The $A_5$ and $\operatorname{SL}_2(\F_5)$ Ferrari refinements retain every CM candidate, with the latter retaining all $864$ points. All $432$ multiplier-one points lift through the full two-adic and three-adic Fermat boundary class-two towers, with exact $\mathbb Z_2^{10}$ and $\mathbb Z_3^{10}$ correction fibres, retaining their degree-six pentagons and generating maps. Explicit finite corrections at both primes fail at the next precision, while every CM fibre remains nonempty. The same word gives compatible identity shadows on every full pro-$p$ boundary factor for $p\ge5$. Every prescribed full boundary family also has a simultaneous generating lift with the double-cover Ferrari refinement through the explicit exponent-twenty comparison. An ordinary order-five peripheral shadow has no generating lift across a specified split $A_6^{20}$ chief extension, for any of its four nonidentity powers, with the admitted pro-five comparison retained. The exponent-three class-three boundary quotient imposes four new congruences on the complete three-adic class-two tower and excludes an explicit tower point, while retaining every CM fibre. The complete $A_6$ kernel and outer-coordinate tests retain all $864$ points. A five-point Hurwitz quotient has pure and full image $A_{96}$; its complete source and explicit exponent-ten boundary comparison retain all those points and the order-five rotation conjugacy. Explicit fully invariant finite five-group targets carry all three compatible ordinary weight-five special parameters, including their exact geometric symmetry. The complete integral three-adic class-three boundary fibre is $\mathbb Z_3^{70}$; its exact exponent-three image has $3^{25}$ points per retained source and excludes a specified finite shadow. Every generating peripheral lift in a universal coprime Frattini cover is parameterized, with its full ordinary centralizer union. The five-strand $\operatorname{Sp}_4(\mathbb F_3)$ test retains every candidate through its actual $G_6$ source quotient. This working manuscript is \textbf{INCOMPLETE}; the task register identifies every unresolved item. We claim no priority.
\end{abstract}
